{UTF-8}
{ Chapter 17: an account management firm. Referrals grow the account base (R1); overloaded staff serve accounts worse, which cuts referrals (B1) and raises losses (B2); hiring towards a workload target restores service (R2 through quality, B3 closing the staff gap) but hiring capacity is limited. }
Referral Rate=
	0.12
	~	1/month
	~	New accounts per month per account, when service is good.
	|
Base Loss Fraction=
	0.01
	~	1/month
	~	|
Extra Loss Fraction=
	0.06
	~	1/month
	~	Additional loss fraction when service fails completely.
	|
Accounts per Person=
	20
	~	accounts/person
	~	|
Workload Tolerance=
	1.3
	~	dmnl
	~	Workload at which half of accounts are served well.
	|
Hiring Time=
	3
	~	month
	~	|
Maximum Hiring=
	1
	~	person/month
	~	What recruiting and onboarding can absorb each month.
	|
Workload=
	Accounts / (Staff * Accounts per Person)
	~	dmnl
	~	|
Service Quality=
	1 / (1 + (Workload / Workload Tolerance) ^ 4)
	~	dmnl
	~	Share of accounts served well.
	|
New Accounts=
	Accounts * Referral Rate * Service Quality
	~	accounts/month
	~	|
Lost Accounts=
	Accounts * (Base Loss Fraction + Extra Loss Fraction * (1 - Service Quality))
	~	accounts/month
	~	|
Desired Staff=
	Accounts / Accounts per Person
	~	person
	~	|
Staff Gap=
	Desired Staff - Staff
	~	person
	~	|
Hiring=
	MIN(Maximum Hiring, MAX(0, Staff Gap / Hiring Time))
	~	person/month
	~	|
Accounts= INTEG(
	New Accounts - Lost Accounts,
	200)
	~	accounts
	~	|
Staff= INTEG(
	Hiring,
	12)
	~	person
	~	|
INITIAL TIME = 0 ~ month ~ |
FINAL TIME = 120 ~ month ~ |
TIME STEP = 0.0625 ~ month ~ |
SAVEPER = 0.0625 ~ month ~ |
